 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\n3. No corresponding meter reading order and no meter reading result exists for the uploaded meter reading result.\n\nIn this case, the key fields for one of the following alternatives must be maintained:\n\no Serial Number, Register, Meter Reading Date\n\nIf the serial number is not unique in the system, a material must also be entered.\no Serial Number, Register, Meter Reading Date\nIf the serial number is not unique in the system, a material number must also be entered.\n\no Point of Delivery, Register, Meter Reading Date\n\nYou can also change the meter reading results using BOR method UPLOAD or BOR object MTRREADDOC. the interface of the\nmethod contains the following parameters:\n\ne MeterReadResChange (for changing meter reading results)\n\ne MeterReadResUpdate (for updating meter reading results)\n\nActivities\nChange Meter Reading Results Using IDoc Category ISU_MR_UPLOADO2\n\n1. Change the meter reading results using IDoc category ISU_LMR_UPLOADOZ2 and fill in segment EIBPEABLUCHANGE with\nthe upload data for the meter reading results to be changed.\n\n2. Import the IDoc into the system and check the log for the upload process (IUPP).\n\nUpdate Meter Reading Results Using IDoc Category ISU_MR_UPLOADO2\n\n1. Update the meter reading results using IDoc category ISU_MR_UPLOADO2 and fill in segment ELBPEABLUUPDATE with the\nupload data for the meter reading results to be updated.\n\n2. Import the IDoc into the system and check the log for the upload process (IUPP).\n\nChange Meter Reading Results Using BOR Method \u2018Upload\u2019 of BOR object \u2018MTRREADDOC\u2019\n\n1. Fill the MeterReadResChange parameter with uploaded data for the meter reading results to be changed.\n\n2. Execute the method.\nUpdate Meter Reading Results Using BOR Method \u2018Upload\u2019 of BOR object \u2018MTRREADDOC\u2019\n\n1. Fill the MeterReadResUpdate parameter with uploaded data for the meter reading results to be updated.\n\n2. Execute the method.\n\nCorrection of Plausible Meter Reading Results\n\nUse\n",
